      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n1. Unused imports (`assertEquals`, `assertNull`, `assertThrows`, `assertTrue`, `UnsupportedCharsetException`, `CharEncoding`, `EncoderException`)\n2. Unused constants (`SWISS_GERMAN_STUFF_UNICODE`, `RUSSIAN_STUFF_UNICODE`) and dead helper method (`constructString`)\n3. The comment on `BASE64_IMPOSSIBLE_CASES` is cryptic — it doesn't explain what makes them \"impossible\" or what the test is verifying\n\nI'll write a cleaner version now.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, dead constants, and the unused helper method, adds clear Javadoc explaining what \"impossible\" Base64 samples are and why lenient decoding matters, renames the loop variable to `encodedWord` for clarity, and adds a descriptive `assertFalse` failure message — all without changing the methods called or their arguments."
